d like yeah mom it's a phase and I'm  gonna let you have that sentence because  I didn't tell you about it I hid it from  you for so long so I'll let you go  through the natural progression of what  a parent thinks when your child comes  out it's a phase they'll get over it  okay I'll let you have it she's still  working with it and I told my dad he was  like I had a feeling I'm like yeah I had  like every pair of Jordans ever of  course not that that means anything but  I mean hello I felt lighter I felt like  I could go out and not have to put on 17  different hats to be myself  so I fell in love  when I realized that just living my  truth of what I am there's one less  person to fight me in my own head I can  get to the problem a little bit more but  art is my passion I can sit in my art  room for hours and not hear one voice  it's kind of like sanctuary for me that  took away even the fight of my sexuality  in my head it's the first time I  actually felt free is with my my  physical art so now when I deal with an  issue with my weight or with a friend or  a family member or something in the  industry it's not that hard as of right  now if I had to speak to someone that  was going through a problem in their  life that feels too large to even deal  with the good news is it will pass  you'll get bumps and bruises but if you  stick through it people forget people  forget and time goes on and hopefully  you learn from it don't stress learn how  to deal with it now that you're young  openness is most important because it  doesn't matter what you see me as and  you label me it's what I label myself  it's funny because when I came out I was  like oh my god I'm gonna die I thought I  was gonna die because when you hold on a  secret for so long like it just keeps  building and building and building and  one day the top is gonna explode over  first of all I thought I lost all my  talent cuz I thought that my secret game  is inside of me was the reason I was so  amazing but